# Template Conventions

## Placeholders

- Format: `{{PLACEHOLDER_NAME}}` — double curly braces, UPPER_SNAKE_CASE.
- Current placeholders: `{{PROJECT_NAME}}`, `{{ROOT_FOLDERS}}`.
- All placeholders must be replaceable by `sed` in `activate.sh`. Avoid characters that conflict with sed delimiters (`|`).

## ai_project_index.toml

- Sections: `[meta]`, `[meta.tech]`, `[structure]`, `[modules]`, `[entry_points]`, `[commands]`, `[boundaries]`, `[dependencies.external]`, `[gotchas]`, `[change_risk]`, `[conventions]`, `[conventions.patterns]`, `[conventions.files]`, `[notes]`.
- Use TOML comments (`#`) for examples and guidance — users and AI fill in values.
- `[[component]]` arrays are for inline component definitions; larger projects use separate module files.

## INIT.md

- Step-by-step AI analysis instructions — maintain the numbered step structure.
- Must be self-contained: an AI reading only this file should understand the full workflow.
- References `ai_project_index/ai_project_index.toml` and `ai_project_index/modules/` as output targets.
